        itemId = 52201,
        name = "Muradin's Favor",
        stepCount = 16,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - A traded reward bypasses Shadowmourne; the personal quest route needs helpers and repeated weekly raids.\n\n1. For the direct route, buy the FINISHED Muradin's Favor (52201) from the Auction House or another player and continue at step 16. Neither Shadowmourne ownership nor its class restrictions apply to a buyer. For your own quest reward, follow steps 2-15.\n\n2. On a Warrior, Paladin or Death Knight, enter 25-player Icecrown Citadel at 53.7, 87.0 in Icecrown. Reach Friendly with the Ashen Verdict by killing raid enemies, then accept The Sacred and the Corrupt from Highlord Darion Mograine on the left inside the entrance (42.6, 22.6 on The Lower Citadel map).\n\n3. With the quest active, travel to Frostmourne Cavern in northeastern Dragonblight (74.4, 23.5). Interact with Light's Vengeance, let the Lich King's scene play, interact again when prompted and defeat the resurrected enemy. Loot the hammer after the sequence; this is the quest object, not a normal world weapon drop.\n\n4. Obtain 25 Primordial Saronite and loot Festergut's Acidic Blood and Rotface's Acidic Blood in the 25-player raid. Their rooms are on The Upper Reaches floor, at 19.8, 65.4 and 19.8, 41.9 respectively. Deliver the components to Darion and finish the runeforge turn-ins to receive Shadow's Edge.\n\n5. For A Feast of Souls, EQUIP Shadow's Edge and collect 50 souls. Apply Shadow's Fate before killing enemies; instant kills can miss credit. A Death Knight can tag with Chains of Ice without attacking, or a Protection Warrior with Demoralizing Shout. Check the debuff and quest counter before clearing more enemies. Disable incidental damage effects that kill targets too soon. Return to Darion for Unholy Infusion when complete.\n\n6. For Unholy Infusion, keep Shadow's Edge equipped and bring a helper to hold Professor Putricide at 13.2, 53.4 on The Upper Reaches. Let several slime puddles form without pushing him through phases. Use his laboratory table to become the abomination, absorb puddles until you have 100 energy, then cast the vehicle's Shadow Infusion ability fully. Only kill Putricide after the infusion is active; the helper prevents him resetting while you are in the vehicle. Turn in the quest before the next infusion.\n\n7. For Blood Infusion, reach Blood-Queen Lana'thel at 51.1, 43.8 on Royal Quarters with Shadow's Edge equipped. Use three same-faction helpers who hold damage, dismiss pets and spread out. An alternative is three of your own same-faction alts: invite them through a custom premade raid, enter the SAME saved instance with the quest character first, and position all four in her room before pulling. Faster loading matters for that alternative.\n\n8. Gain Blood Mirror so Gushing Wound applies, and obtain Essence of the Blood Queen on the quest character. Keep a helper close enough for the mirror link until it appears. For the alt method, body-pull on the quest character, reconnect into alt 1, then immediately reconnect back to the quest character; the disconnected alt remains available to bite. Two windowed game clients avoid repeatedly waiting for a full client restart. Temporarily disable slow-loading addons through the character-selection AddOns menu if needed.\n\n9. Wait for Essence's timer to expire, target the first unbitten helper/alt and use Vampiric Bite from the temporary action bar immediately. Confirm the bite landed. Repeat for a SECOND and THIRD different target when the timer returns. With your own alts, reconnect into alt 2 and back before bite two, then alt 3 and back before bite three. Use low-damage alts first so mind control does not kill the remaining targets; keep the final alt sturdy enough to survive.\n\n10. Count THREE successful bites, then kill Lana'thel while still wielding Shadow's Edge. The quest credit arrives after her death, so lack of an early completion popup is not failure. If the setup fails, reset the encounter while she is alive; killing her prematurely spends that character's weekly opportunity. Return to Darion and take Frost Infusion before touching Sindragosa.\n\n11. For Frost Infusion, reach Sindragosa at 36.6, 23.4 on The Frost Queen's Lair map. Keep Shadow's Edge equipped, face her breath and survive FOUR Frost Breaths before finishing her. Hold damage and heal through the waiting period; killing her before the fourth breath means waiting for another eligible weekly kill.\n\n12. Turn in the infusion and accept The Splintered Throne. Collect 50 Shadowfrost Shards from eligible 25-player Icecrown boss kills over weekly resets. The shards are quest drops; bought Primordial Saronite cannot replace them. Finish Darion's forging quests to receive Shadowmourne.\n\n13. Accept The Lich King's Last Stand. With the finished Shadowmourne equipped, defeat the Lich King on The Frozen Throne (49.9, 52.8) in the 25-player raid and loot the Sealed Chest. This reward is once per eligible legendary quest chain; ordinary weekly kills with an already-finished Shadowmourne do not generate unlimited chests.\n\n14. Use the raid's transporters to return to The Lower Citadel. Bring the chest to Darion (42.6, 22.6) for Personal Property and open the Unsealed Chest. It contains the keepsakes for ALL five follow-up rewards; choosing one does not forfeit the others.\n\n15. Take Arthas' Training Sword from that container and use it to start Muradin's Lament. Speak to Muradin Bronzebeard among the post-victory NPCs near the raid entrance. This is the friendly ICC version, even for the opposite faction. Do not travel to a capital-city version of the character. Wait for one reward's scene to finish before turning in another keepsake. If the NPCs are missing on a later visit, finish the Lich King again in that instance to restore the victory phase.\n\n16. Use Muradin's Favor from your bags to add it to the account-wide Toy Box. If you bought the finished toy, no chest, keepsake delivery or legendary quest is needed. An unused reward can be traded; a learned Toy Box entry cannot be sold.",
